  "id": "wf4-verify-recipient-changed-after-the-gate",
  "description": "If the Approval Gate resolved a different recipient than the verified register row, the branch halts before any send.",
  "why_it_exists": "On the real MAT-20260101-002 snapshot the Actions register held TWO generations of rows written 39 minutes apart, so six action_ids each resolved to two rows carrying different action_types, recipients and channels. Approval Gate re-queried by action_id and simply took the last match, meaning WF4 could draft, approve and send against a row nobody chose - for example sending a CONTACT_INSURER letter to a car park manager. The Integrity Guard refuses to choose between duplicate rows, and Verify Selected Row re-checks the chosen row immediately before any writer or Gmail node runs. The recipient is one of the two fields that decide where an external message physically goes, so it is re-checked against the register immediately before the Gmail nodes.",
